answer.worked:
Line $C$ crosses the $y$-axis at $(0,3)$, so the $y$-intercept is $3$. It also passes through $(2,2)$, so the gradient is
$$\begin{align*}
m&=\frac{2-3}{2-0}\\
&=-\frac{1}{2}
\end{align*}$$
Therefore
$$\begin{align*}
y&=-\frac{1}{2}x+3
\end{align*}$$

$$\begin{align*}
4x + 2y &= 8 \\
4x &= 8 - 2y \\
x &= \frac{8 - 2y}{4} \\
x &= \frac{4 - y}{2}
\end{align*}$$

